BFS (Breadth-First Search)
Start from the selected node.
Mark the node as visited and add it to a queue.
Remove a node from the queue and display it.
Add its unvisited adjacent nodes to the queue.
Repeat until the queue is empty.
Check whether the target file was found.


DFS (Depth-First Search)
Start from the selected node.
Mark the node as visited and display it.
Visit an unvisited adjacent node recursively.
Continue until no unvisited adjacent nodes remain.
Backtrack and visit other unvisited nodes.
Check whether the target file was found.
